3)Crimping Tool:
A crimping tool is a handy device that allows you to create secure connections between
wires and connectors. It works by deforming the connector onto the wire, ensuring a
strong bond. With a crimping tool, you can easily join electrical wires, network cables,
coaxial cables, and more.
4)Crimping RJ45 Connector on Cat6 Cable:
Untwist and Arrange the Pairs:
 Untwist the twisted pairs of wires carefully and arrange them in the appropriate order
according to the wiring standard you are using (T568A or T568B).
 The typical order for each pair is:
 Pair 1 (Blue/White Blue)
 Pair 2 (Orange/White Orange)
 Pair 3 (Green/White Green)
 Pair 4 (Brown/White Brown)
Insert Wires into RJ45 Connector
Trim Excess Wires
Crimp the Connector
